  "delivered_messages_sha256": "b16a71ebc6be772fc2271cc8ac6fffeb23cc33dd70ffb78e451baf6db674505f",
  "raw_text": "No. Timing alone establishes correlation, not causation.\n\nTo establish causation, you would need additional evidence, such as:\n\n- Error logs linking the failure to the update\n- A reproducible failure after installing the update\n- The problem disappearing after rollback\n- A known defect in the update that could cause that failure\n- Elimination of other plausible causes, such as hardware wear, power issues, or operator error\n\nThe fact that the machine failed one day later may justify investigation, but it does not by itself prove the update caused the failure.",
